{"type":"Environment","id":"free_728f0aebbdcb-88e17a8abe1a","meta":{"status":"ready","error":null},"title":"Doppler effect: an ambulance driving past","lane":"free","label":"model-checked","kitVersion":"0.1.0","htmlSha256":"88e17a8abe1adaef9c574b8cc3da14d2b3a4d3017080472f72a74d153b02dd62","html":"<!doctype html><html lang=\"en\"><head>\n<meta http-equiv=\"Content-Security-Policy\" content=\"default-src 'none'; script-src 'unsafe-inline' http://localhost:3001/vendor/; style-src 'unsafe-inline'; img-src data:; font-src http://localhost:3001/vendor/ data:; connect-src 'none'; frame-src 'none'; object-src 'none'; base-uri 'none'; form-action 'none';\"><meta charset=\"utf-8\"><meta name=\"viewport\" content=\"width=device-width, initial-scale=1\"><title>Doppler effect: an ambulance driving past</title><style>\n:root{--bg:#ffffff;--fg:#2f3a34;--muted:#4f5d57;--accent:#0a776b;--card:#f7f8f4;--border:#d3dace;--bench:#fbfcf8;--try:#8a3340;--step:#6b4aa0;--gold:#8f6100;--goldsoft:#fff8e6;--goldborder:#ecd9a6;color-scheme:light}\n@media (prefers-color-scheme: dark){:root:not([data-theme=\"light\"]){--bg:#16201c;--fg:#e9efea;--muted:#a4b2ab;--accent:#16b6a3;--card:#0e1512;--border:#34403a;--bench:#121a16;--try:#f0a3ad;--step:#b9a0e6;--gold:#e8b84a;--goldsoft:#2a2414;--goldborder:#5a4a1c;color-scheme:dark}}\n:root[data-theme=\"dark\"]{--bg:#16201c;--fg:#e9efea;--muted:#a4b2ab;--accent:#16b6a3;--card:#0e1512;--border:#34403a;--bench:#121a16;--try:#f0a3ad;--step:#b9a0e6;--gold:#e8b84a;--goldsoft:#2a2414;--goldborder:#5a4a1c;color-scheme:dark}\n*{box-sizing:border-box}\nbody{margin:0;background:var(--bg);color:var(--fg);font:16px/1.55 system-ui,-apple-system,\"Segoe UI\",sans-serif}\nmain.lab{max-width:1100px;margin:0 auto;padding:16px;display:grid;gap:14px}\n.kicker{margin:0;font:700 .75rem/1.2 ui-monospace,Consolas,monospace;letter-spacing:.14em;text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--accent)}\nh1{margin:.2rem 0 .3rem;font-size:1.6rem;line-height:1.2}\nh2{margin:0 0 .4rem;font-size:1rem;letter-spacing:.02em}\n.try{margin:0;padding:10px 14px;border-left:4px solid var(--try);background:var(--card);border-radius:10px}\n.try strong{color:var(--try)}\n.card{background:var(--card);border:2px solid var(--border);border-radius:18px;padding:10px 16px}\n.idea{background:var(--goldsoft);border-color:var(--goldborder)}\n.idea h2{color:var(--gold)}\n.idea p{margin:.2rem 0}\n.top{display:grid;gap:14px;grid-template-columns:1fr}\n.steps ol{margin:0;padding-left:1.4rem}\n.steps li{padding-left:2px}\n.predict ul{margin:.2rem 0 .4rem;padding-left:1.2rem}\nsummary{cursor:pointer;min-height:44px;display:flex;align-items:center;font-weight:600;color:var(--accent)}\n.benchrow{display:grid;gap:14px;grid-template-columns:1fr}\n.bench{background:var(--bench);border:2px solid var(--border);border-radius:18px;padding:8px;overflow:hidden}\n.bench svg{display:block;width:100%;height:auto;max-height:520px;touch-action:none}\n.side{display:grid;gap:12px;align-content:start}\n.readouts{display:grid;gap:10px;grid-template-columns:repeat(auto-fit,minmax(140px,1fr))}\n.readout{background:var(--card);border:2px solid var(--border);border-radius:14px;padding:8px 12px}\n.readout .name{font-size:.85rem;color:var(--muted)}\n.readout output{display:block;font-size:1.35rem;font-weight:700;font-variant-numeric:tabular-nums}\n.found{margin:0;border-color:var(--accent)}\n.found:empty{display:none}\n.fine summary{font-size:.9rem;color:var(--muted)}\n.row{display:grid;grid-template-columns:minmax(90px,auto) 1fr;align-items:center;gap:10px;min-height:44px}\n.row label{font-size:.9rem;color:var(--muted)}\n.row input[type=range]{width:100%;min-height:44px;accent-color:var(--accent)}\n.hints details{border-top:1px solid var(--border)}\n.hints details:first-of-type{border-top:0}\n.explain p{margin:.3rem 0}\n@media (min-width:760px){.top{grid-template-columns:1.2fr 1fr}.benchrow{grid-template-columns:minmax(0,1.6fr) minmax(260px,1fr)}}\n\n#bench-art .lab{font-size:14px;fill:var(--fg)}\n#bench-art .mut{font-size:12px;fill:var(--muted)}\n#bench-art .big{font-size:15px;font-weight:bold;fill:var(--fg)}\n#bench-art #rings circle{fill:none;stroke:var(--accent);stroke-width:2}\n#bench-art #wave{fill:none;stroke:var(--accent);stroke-width:2.5}</style></head><body><main class=\"lab\"><header><p class=\"kicker\">Physics, Form 4</p><h1>Doppler effect: an ambulance driving past</h1><p class=\"try\"><strong>Try this:</strong> Drag the ambulance along the road from left to right, past you, and listen with your eyes to the pitch readout.</p></header><div class=\"top\"><section class=\"card idea\"><h2>Key idea</h2><p>Sound waves bunch up in front of a moving source and stretch out behind it, so the pitch you hear changes.</p><p>f_heard = f_siren x v / (v - u), where u is the source&#x27;s speed towards you</p></section><section class=\"card predict\"><h2>Predict first</h2><p>The siren always makes the same note. What will you hear as the ambulance drives towards you, passes, and drives away?</p><ul><li>The same pitch all the time</li><li>Higher while it approaches, then lower once it has passed</li><li>Lower while it approaches, then higher once it has passed</li></ul><details><summary>Check your prediction</summary><p>Set the speed to 25 m/s, drag the ambulance from far left to far right, and watch the &quot;Pitch you hear&quot; readout.</p></details></section></div><section class=\"card steps\"><h2>Steps</h2><ol><li>Drag the ambulance to the far left and read the pitch you hear. Look at how the circles are squeezed together in front of it.</li><li>Drag the ambulance slowly along the road until it is directly opposite you. Watch the pitch fall to the siren&#x27;s true 700 Hz.</li><li>Keep dragging to the right. The circles are now spread out behind the ambulance and the pitch is lower than 700 Hz.</li><li>Drag the speed knob at the top to 60 m/s and then to 0 m/s. See how the pitch change grows and then vanishes.</li></ol></section><section class=\"benchrow\" aria-label=\"The lab bench\"><div class=\"bench\"><svg id=\"bench-art\" viewBox=\"0 0 640 350\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Ambulance on a road with sound waves and a listener\">\n<rect width=\"640\" height=\"350\" fill=\"var(--bench)\"/>\n<text class=\"lab\" x=\"20\" y=\"37\">Speed</text>\n<line x1=\"100\" y1=\"32\" x2=\"540\" y2=\"32\" stroke=\"var(--border)\" stroke-width=\"6\" stroke-linecap=\"round\"/>\n<text class=\"big\" id=\"spdtxt\" x=\"568\" y=\"37\">25 m/s</text>\n<rect x=\"0\" y=\"186\" width=\"640\" height=\"28\" fill=\"var(--card)\" stroke=\"var(--border)\"/>\n<line x1=\"0\" y1=\"200\" x2=\"640\" y2=\"200\" stroke=\"var(--muted)\" stroke-dasharray=\"14 10\"/>\n<g id=\"rings\"></g>\n<line id=\"ray\" x1=\"0\" y1=\"0\" x2=\"0\" y2=\"0\" stroke=\"var(--muted)\" stroke-dasharray=\"4 4\"/>\n<g id=\"amb\">\n<rect x=\"-34\" y=\"-26\" width=\"68\" height=\"26\" rx=\"5\" fill=\"#ffffff\" stroke=\"var(--fg)\" stroke-width=\"2\"/>\n<rect x=\"14\" y=\"-22\" width=\"16\" height=\"10\" fill=\"#9fd3f5\"/>\n<rect x=\"-30\" y=\"-14\" width=\"40\" height=\"5\" fill=\"#d62828\"/>\n<circle id=\"light\" cx=\"0\" cy=\"-30\" r=\"5\" fill=\"#d62828\"/>\n<circle cx=\"-18\" cy=\"0\" r=\"6\" fill=\"var(--fg)\"/>\n<circle cx=\"18\" cy=\"0\" r=\"6\" fill=\"var(--fg)\"/>\n<text class=\"mut\" x=\"-26\" y=\"22\">Ambulance</text>\n<rect x=\"-48\" y=\"-48\" width=\"96\" height=\"76\" fill=\"var(--bench)\" fill-opacity=\"0.01\" data-synapse-handle=\"pos\" aria-hidden=\"true\" style=\"touch-action:none;cursor:grab\"/>\n</g>\n<g>\n<circle cx=\"320\" cy=\"246\" r=\"9\" fill=\"var(--card)\" stroke=\"var(--fg)\" stroke-width=\"2\"/>\n<line x1=\"320\" y1=\"255\" x2=\"320\" y2=\"280\" stroke=\"var(--fg)\" stroke-width=\"3\"/>\n<line x1=\"320\" y1=\"262\" x2=\"306\" y2=\"274\" stroke=\"var(--fg)\" stroke-width=\"3\"/>\n<line x1=\"320\" y1=\"262\" x2=\"334\" y2=\"274\" stroke=\"var(--fg)\" stroke-width=\"3\"/>\n<text class=\"lab\" x=\"345\" y=\"262\">You (listener)</text>\n</g>\n<text class=\"mut\" x=\"20\" y=\"302\">Sound wave reaching your ear</text>\n<path id=\"wave\" d=\"M40 325 L600 325\"/>\n<g id=\"knob\" transform=\"translate(240,32)\">\n<circle r=\"12\" fill=\"var(--accent)\" stroke=\"var(--fg)\" stroke-width=\"2\"/>\n<circle r=\"40\" fill=\"var(--bench)\" fill-opacity=\"0.01\" data-synapse-handle=\"speed\" aria-hidden=\"true\" style=\"touch-action:none;cursor:grab\"/>\n</g>\n</svg></div><div class=\"side\"><div class=\"readouts\"><div class=\"readout\"><div class=\"name\" id=\"heard-name\">Pitch you hear (Hz)</div><output id=\"heard\" data-synapse-readout=\"heard\" aria-labelledby=\"heard-name\"></output></div><div class=\"readout\"><div class=\"name\" id=\"shift-name\">Change from the siren&#x27;s 700 Hz (Hz)</div><output id=\"shift\" data-synapse-readout=\"shift\" aria-labelledby=\"shift-name\"></output></div><div class=\"readout\"><div class=\"name\" id=\"radial-name\">Speed towards you (m/s)</div><output id=\"radial\" data-synapse-readout=\"radial\" aria-labelledby=\"radial-name\"></output></div><div class=\"readout\"><div class=\"name\" id=\"dist-name\">Distance to you (m)</div><output id=\"dist\" data-synapse-readout=\"dist\" aria-labelledby=\"dist-name\"></output></div></div><p id=\"found\" class=\"card found\" aria-live=\"polite\"></p><details class=\"card fine\"><summary>Keyboard controls</summary><div class=\"row\"><label for=\"pos\">Ambulance position (0 = opposite you)</label><input type=\"range\" id=\"pos\" data-synapse-control=\"pos\" min=\"-100\" max=\"100\" step=\"1\" value=\"-80\" data-unit=\"m\" aria-valuetext=\"-80 m\"></div><div class=\"row\"><label for=\"speed\">Ambulance speed</label><input type=\"range\" id=\"speed\" data-synapse-control=\"speed\" min=\"0\" max=\"80\" step=\"1\" value=\"25\" data-unit=\"m/s\" aria-valuetext=\"25 m/s\"></div></details></div></section><section class=\"card hints\"><h2>Need a hint?</h2><details><summary>Hint 1</summary><p>Compare the spacing of the circles in front of the ambulance with the spacing behind it.</p></details><details><summary>Hint 2</summary><p>Only the part of the ambulance&#x27;s speed that points straight at you matters. Look at the &quot;Speed towards you&quot; readout.</p></details><details><summary>Hint 3</summary><p>When the ambulance is opposite you, none of its motion is towards or away from you, so you hear the true 700 Hz.</p></details></section><section class=\"explain\"><h2>Why it happens</h2><p>Each circle on the drawing is a sound wave sent out by the siren at an earlier moment. The ambulance keeps moving after sending each one, so in front of it the waves are squeezed closer together and behind it they are stretched apart. Closer waves mean a shorter wavelength, so more waves reach your ear each second and the pitch is higher.</p><p>Only the part of the ambulance&#x27;s velocity along the line to you counts. This is the &quot;Speed towards you&quot; readout, u. Far away on the road it is almost the full speed. Directly opposite you it is zero. After that it is negative, because the ambulance is moving away. The heard frequency is f = f_siren x v / (v - u), with the speed of sound v = 340 m/s and f_siren = 700 Hz.</p><p>The siren itself never changes note. The drop in pitch as the ambulance passes happens because the ambulance changes from approaching to receding. The faster the ambulance, the bigger the change. A stationary ambulance gives no change at all.</p></section></main><script>\naddEventListener(\"message\", function (e) {\n  var d = e.data;\n  if (d && typeof d === \"object\" && d.type === \"synapse_theme\" && (d.theme === \"light\" || d.theme === \"dark\")) document.documentElement.setAttribute(\"data-theme\", d.theme);\n});\nArray.prototype.forEach.call(document.querySelectorAll(\"input[data-synapse-control]\"), function (el) {\n  function say() { el.setAttribute(\"aria-valuetext\", el.value + (el.dataset.unit ? \" \" + el.dataset.unit : \"\")); }\n  el.addEventListener(\"input\", say);\n  say();\n});\n\n(function () {\nvar svg = document.getElementById(\"bench-art\");\nvar NS = svg.namespaceURI;\nfunction $(i) { return document.getElementById(i); }\nvar V_SOUND_MS = 340;\nvar F_SIREN_HZ = 700;\nvar ROAD_GAP_M = 20;\nfunction towardsMS(xM, sMS) {\n  var rM = Math.sqrt(xM * xM + ROAD_GAP_M * ROAD_GAP_M);\n  return sMS * (-xM) / rM;\n}\nfunction heardHz(uMS) { return F_SIREN_HZ * V_SOUND_MS / (V_SOUND_MS - uMS); }\nfunction toSvg(e) {\n  var p = svg.createSVGPoint();\n  p.x = e.clientX; p.y = e.clientY;\n  return p.matrixTransform(svg.getScreenCTM().inverse());\n}\nfunction drag(h, id, f) {\n  var down = false;\n  h.addEventListener(\"pointerdown\", function (e) {\n    h.setPointerCapture(e.pointerId);\n    down = true; h.style.cursor = \"grabbing\"; e.preventDefault();\n  });\n  h.addEventListener(\"pointermove\", function (e) {\n    if (!down) return;\n    var c = $(id);\n    var st = +c.step, mn = +c.min, mx = +c.max;\n    var v = f(toSvg(e));\n    v = Math.round((v - mn) / st) * st + mn;\n    v = Math.max(mn, Math.min(mx, v));\n    c.value = v;\n    c.dispatchEvent(new Event(\"input\", { bubbles: true }));\n  });\n  function up() { down = false; h.style.cursor = \"grab\"; }\n  h.addEventListener(\"pointerup\", up);\n  h.addEventListener(\"pointercancel\", up);\n}\ndrag(svg.querySelector('[data-synapse-handle=\"pos\"]'), \"pos\", function (q) { return (q.x - 320) / 2.8; });\ndrag(svg.querySelector('[data-synapse-handle=\"speed\"]'), \"speed\", function (q) { return (q.x - 100) / 440 * 80; });\nfunction update() {\n  var xM = +$(\"pos\").value;\n  var sMS = +$(\"speed\").value;\n  var px = 320 + xM * 2.8;\n  var uMS = towardsMS(xM, sMS);\n  var fHz = heardHz(uMS);\n  var rM = Math.sqrt(xM * xM + ROAD_GAP_M * ROAD_GAP_M);\n  $(\"amb\").setAttribute(\"transform\", \"translate(\" + px + \",200)\");\n  $(\"knob\").setAttribute(\"transform\", \"translate(\" + (100 + sMS / 80 * 440) + \",32)\");\n  $(\"spdtxt\").textContent = sMS.toFixed(0) + \" m/s\";\n  var ray = $(\"ray\");\n  ray.setAttribute(\"x1\", px); ray.setAttribute(\"y1\", 172);\n  ray.setAttribute(\"x2\", 320); ray.setAttribute(\"y2\", 236);\n  var g = $(\"rings\");\n  while (g.firstChild) g.removeChild(g.firstChild);\n  for (var k = 1; k <= 7; k++) {\n    var rad = k * 28;\n    var c = document.createElementNS(NS, \"circle\");\n    c.setAttribute(\"cx\", px - sMS / V_SOUND_MS * rad);\n    c.setAttribute(\"cy\", 172);\n    c.setAttribute(\"r\", rad);\n    c.setAttribute(\"opacity\", (1 - k * 0.11).toFixed(2));\n    g.appendChild(c);\n  }\n  var lamMs = 40 * F_SIREN_HZ / fHz;\n  var d = \"\";\n  for (var x = 40; x <= 600; x += 4) {\n    var y = 325 + 9 * Math.sin(2 * Math.PI * (x - 40) / lamMs);\n    d += (x === 40 ? \"M\" : \"L\") + x + \" \" + y.toFixed(1) + \" \";\n  }\n  $(\"wave\").setAttribute(\"d\", d);\n  $(\"heard\").textContent = fHz.toFixed(0) + \" Hz\";\n  $(\"shift\").textContent = (fHz - F_SIREN_HZ).toFixed(0) + \" Hz\";\n  $(\"radial\").textContent = uMS.toFixed(1) + \" m/s\";\n  $(\"dist\").textContent = rM.toFixed(0) + \" m\";\n  var state = uMS > 0.5 ? \"approaching\" : (uMS < -0.5 ? \"moving away\" : \"level with you\");\n  $(\"found\").textContent = \"The ambulance is \" + rM.toFixed(0) + \" m away and \" + state + \", so you hear \" + fHz.toFixed(0) + \" Hz instead of 700 Hz.\";\n  svg.setAttribute(\"aria-label\", \"Ambulance \" + state + \" at \" + sMS + \" m/s, \" + rM.toFixed(0) + \" m from the listener, who hears \" + fHz.toFixed(0) + \" Hz\");\n}\n$(\"pos\").addEventListener(\"input\", update);\n$(\"speed\").addEventListener(\"input\", update);\nupdate();\n})();</script></body></html>","citations":[{"source":"UNVERIFIED (no textbook page has been checked for this Environment)","page":null,"quote":null,"verified":false,"printedPage":null}],"checked":{"layers":["postprocess","scan","render","wording"],"controlsExercised":2,"gridPoints":0,"referenceCases":0,"readouts":4,"models":[],"limits":"Written whole by a model and not built on the Kit, so none of its numbers or formulas were compared with an audited science model. Code checked that it runs and that its controls work and a second model read its words and formulas, but only for a short, scripted stretch of time. No textbook source was checked and a person has not reviewed it. Check it against your textbook."},"planSummary":"A page written whole by a model for a question the Kit could not express (topic physics_form4_waves)."}